+### 6.14 Post subgraph (`app/agents/post/`, B2-10)
+
+- `make_post_subgraph(writer=, image=, hashtag=)` returns the compiled subgraph `START -> writer -> image -> hashtag -> END`, each step a checked node (6.3). Pass it as `build_graph(post_subgraph=...)`; it inherits the parent's checkpointer, so an escalation inside it pauses and resumes with the run. `make_writer_node`, `make_image_node` and `make_hashtag_node` return `CheckedNode`s (step keys `writer`, `image`, `hashtag`) and take `max_retries` and `platform_rules` (and `judge_threshold`, `use_judge`, `banned_words` where they apply) from the worker (B3). An aborted escalation ends the subgraph with `status="failed"`. `rerun_from` is not read yet (B2-11).
+- Every step handles all distinct target platforms in one attempt (FR-5.5) and merges into `drafts[platform]`: writer sets `caption` and `title` (a stale title is removed), image replaces the `image` entry of `media` (other media are kept), hashtag sets `hashtags`. Rules, banned words and strategy are read on every run. A missing caption or strategy is a bug (`ValueError`), not a retry.
+- **writer** (`WriterOutput`, temperature 0.8): checks are caption present, within `caption_max` (else `description_max`) and within +-30 % of `strategy.length_target`, no banned word, no `#tag`, raw URL or placeholder in the body, `title` required (and at most `title_max`) for YouTube and empty elsewhere. `refused=true` escalates at once with `"<platform>: <reason>"`. The judge (`kind="fast"`) rubric `WRITER_RUBRIC` carries the research notes.
+- **image** (`ImagePrompt`, temperature 0.7): the prompt's aspect ratio is moved to an allowed one, `get_image_provider().generate(prompt, size)` runs with `1024` on the short side, `get_storage_backend().put` stores the bytes under `requests/<request_id>/<platform>/image-<attempt>.<ext>` and the draft gets `{"type": "image", "storage_key", "meta": {prompt, aspect_ratio, alt_text, style_notes, provider, size_bytes, mime_type, width, height}}` (the `media_assets` table arrives in B3). The checks read the stored bytes back (valid image, size, short side, real aspect ratio) and check the alt text; the judge (`IMAGE_RUBRIC`) is text-only (prompt + alt text against the caption).
+- **hashtag** (`HashtagOutput`, temperature 0.5): rule-only. Tags are `#` + letters/digits/`_`, at most 40 characters, unique ignoring case, within `hashtags_min`/`hashtags_max`, none banned.
+- Limits that are node parameters until B3 reads `system_settings`: `min_short_side` (1024) and `max_image_bytes` (8 MiB) for the image, `use_judge`, `judge_threshold`, `max_retries`.
